• /Context_Library/<key>/subtopics — MAP<string, object>
  value.props: id:string, title:string, content:string, subtopics:map<string, undefined>
  e.g. add → manageMemory { "ops":[{ "action":"add","path":"/Context_Library/<key>/subtopics","key":"<key>","value": {} }] }
• /Context_Library/<key>/subtopics/<key>/subtopics — MAP<string, undefined>
  e.g. add → manageMemory { "ops":[{ "action":"add","path":"/Context_Library/<key>/subtopics/<key>/subtopics","key":"<key>","value": null }] }

Notes:
- When item/value is an OBJECT, include all listed "required" keys when creating it.
- Arrays/maps may enforce limits (uniqueItems, min/max counts) and map keys may have regex constraints.
- For topics, "value" may be a string (description) or a full node {description?, subtopics?}.
